        <briefdescription>
<para>Decompose a dense embedding vector into TT-format. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>embedding</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Dense float32 embedding from a prior <computeroutput>chunk_embed</computeroutput> step. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>chunk_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Identifier linking result to the originating chunk. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>source_file_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>SHA-256 digest of the originating file. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>epsilon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Relative reconstruction error tolerance ε ∈ (0, 1]. Passed directly to <computeroutput>TensorTrainDecomposer</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>max_rank</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Hard bond-dimension cap (0 = no cap). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Populated <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1ingestion_1_1_tensor_core_record" kindref="compound">TensorCoreRecord</ref></computeroutput>. On error, returns a record with empty <computeroutput>serialized_train</computeroutput> so callers can degrade gracefully. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
